// Axis canonical registry.
//
// Identities: §5b bootstrap rule — SHA-256 of the UTF-8 function name bytes.
// New user-defined functions MUST use entropy-minted identities instead.
//
// This is the single semantic source. Surface registries are generated
// projections of this file, not peers that can diverge from it.
//
// Vocabulary is in active development; callable contents will stabilise at v1.0.0.

registry axis 0.5

// ─────────── primitive types ───────────
//
// TYPES: axis-types.axreg owns Unit, Bool, Int, Text, Value, Dec, ValueList
// and Fn. They were declared here until AXREG_LAYERING_VALUE_OWNERSHIP_V1
// was actually enforced in the files; declaring any of them here again is a
// hard load error (duplicate type name), not a shadow or an override.
//
// Two of them did not survive as declared HERE. This file's
//   type Value     = prim value       (id 212f4f49…)
//   type ValueList = list Value       (id 47b62fb6…)
// differed from axis-bridge.axreg's closed-sum Value (23945287…) and its
// ValueList (f6673941…). axis-types.axreg carries the BRIDGE definitions,
// because this file declares zero fns — nothing referenced the `prim value`
// variant, while 411 bridge fns reference the sum. See axis-types.axreg.

